card.statement:
Assume that $Z=y_{k_1}^{-\gamma_1}\dots y_{k_n}^{-\gamma_n}y_{j_1}^{\beta_1}\ldots y_{j_l}^{\beta_l}x_{i_1}^{\alpha_1}\ldots x_{i_k}^{\alpha_k}$, where $p, \gamma_1,\ldots,\gamma_n,$ $\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_l,$ $\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_k\in\mathbb N$. Then

\begin{equation*}
e_{-i}(x_i^{-p}Z)=A_{\alpha,p}x_i^{-p-1}Z+x_i^{-p}Z'+x_i^{-p+1}Z''
\end{equation*}

in $M_{i,S}$, where $\alpha=\displaystyle\sum_{s=1}^k\alpha_s = \deg_{x^+} (x_i^{-p}Z)$, and $Z'$ and $Z''$ are $\deg_{x^+}$-homogeneous polynomials which are either zero in $M_{i,S}$ or $\deg_{x^+}(x_i^{-p+1}Z'')=\deg_{x^+}(x_i^{-p}Z')-1=\alpha-2$. In particular, $f_ie_{-i}(x_i^{-1}Z)=A_{\alpha,1}x_i^{-1}Z$.
